# Shake To Delete — an iOS-like 4x6 grid of metallic app tiles: a long press
# toggles "jiggle" mode (per-tile randomised withRepeat rotation/translate) and
# shows "-" badges; tapping a badge stops the jiggle and removes that tile
# (FadeOut + LinearTransition reflow).
# What this test covers: entering jiggle mode, deleting a tile from the first
# row and from the last row (reflow), toggling jiggle on/off with two long
# presses, deleting while the jiggle is just starting, two badge taps in quick
# succession (second lands while the first delete is pending), tapping badges
# while not jiggling (must do nothing), and leaving jiggle mode off.
# NOTE: isShaking is a module-level makeMutable, so closing the demo while
# jiggling reopens it already jiggling; the first badge tap below normalises
# that (it deletes a tile only if jiggling). See report.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/shake-to-delete"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 45000
# Warm-up touch on the status bar: the first touch of a test can be lost while
# the XCTest runner attaches.
press 330 20
wait 500
wait 1500
# Normalise: tile 2's badge (works only if already jiggling).
press 220 81
wait 1200
# Jiggle on, delete tile 2 (badge at tile centre -24,-25).
longpress 148 300 800
wait 1200
press 124 81
wait 1500
# Jiggle on, delete a tile in the last row.
longpress 148 300 800
wait 1200
press 124 561
wait 1500
# Toggle on and off with two long presses.
longpress 244 394 800
wait 1000
longpress 244 394 800
wait 1000
# Not jiggling: badge taps must be ignored.
press 220 177
wait 500
press 316 273
wait 800
# Jiggle on and delete immediately, then a second badge 100ms later.
longpress 52 490 800
press 220 177
wait 100
press 316 273
wait 1500
# Scrolling area below the grid (no ScrollView): tap empty space.
press 200 750
wait 800
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
